# Hosts and patterns that lychee should not attempt to verify.
# Keep this list narrow — broken external links are usually worth
# learning about, not silencing.

# Placeholder hosts commonly used in examples
^https?://example\.(com|org|net)/?
^https?://localhost(:[0-9]+)?/?
^https?://127\.0\.0\.1(:[0-9]+)?/?

# Bot-hostile hosts that frequently return 403/429 to scrapers
^https?://(www\.)?linkedin\.com/
^https?://(www\.)?x\.com/
^https?://twitter\.com/

# GitHub's own anchor-only fragments lychee can't always resolve
^#$

# Our future render surface — wired up alongside v0.1.0 content; until
# then the link is correct but the page 404s. Re-enable once docs-hub
# mounts /supply-chain/.
^https://docs\.ozarksecuritylabs\.com/supply-chain/?$

# scorecard.dev (the entire host, not just /viewer/) has had connection
# failures during sustained outages where lychee's retry budget can't
# recover. The api.scorecard.dev endpoint (which serves the badge image)
# is a different host and stays in-scope; only the human-facing
# scorecard.dev pages are excluded.
^https://scorecard\.dev/

# slsa.dev has had multiple sustained outages where even our maxed-out
# retry budget (6 attempts, 30s timeout each, 10s backoff) hits
# "Connection failed" on every attempt. The spec URLs themselves are
# stable references — verify the link manually when authoring; trust
# slsa.dev to be the canonical source even when its host is flapping.
^https://slsa\.dev/
